fix: union projection members with official byId subagents + drop ghost lead

Live console diagnostics delivered the picture: empty-state fired with
byIdTotal 0 (byId not hydrated yet on first render) and body state showed
n 1 with a single member literally named lead at the center — the live
agentTeam projection contains a ghost lead entry, and subagent-tool
sessions never enter agentTeam.members, so the star graph collapsed to one
dot.

- members = projection members (ghost entries with id equal to the lead
  removed) UNION buildOfficialTeams(byId)[leadId] (deduped by id), so the
  star ring always equals projection plus the official session-directory
  subagents — even when the projection is non-empty
- layout effect now keys on memberSig (leadId plus member id list) so a
  later byId hydration that adds subagents reloads the layout
- diagnostics are hydration-aware: empty-state may re-log up to 4 times
  while byId is still empty; body diagnostic gains byIdTotal/officialSubs
- e2e: 43/43 TRUE
